Skip the BSD libc resolver fallback in TQDns::doResInit() on substrate.

substrate's libc declares res_init()/__res_state() in <resolv.h> but
provides no implementation, so linking any executable against
libtqt-mt.so failed with undefined references to res_init and
__res_state (the latter via the _res macro = (*__res_state())).

doResInit() already parses /etc/resolv.conf by hand as its primary
source of nameservers; the libc-resolver block is only a fallback when
that file yields nothing.  Compile that fallback out on substrate so we
rely on the manual parse alone.

--- a/src/network/qdns.cpp
+++ b/src/network/qdns.cpp
@@ -2592,7 +2592,10 @@
     }
 
     if (ns->isEmpty()) {
-#if defined(Q_MODERN_RES_API)
+#if defined(__substrate__)
+	/* substrate has no BSD libc resolver (res_init/res_ninit/_res);
+	   nameservers come solely from the /etc/resolv.conf parse above. */
+#elif defined(Q_MODERN_RES_API)
 	struct __res_state res;
 	/* the storage must be clean */
 	memset(&res, 0, sizeof(res));
